1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,547
So our gathering today has a name,

2
00:00:02,547 --> 00:00:04,311
and it's called "Your Sins Are Forgiven."

3
00:00:04,311 --> 00:00:06,662
You might find that a bit abrupt —

4
00:00:06,662 --> 00:00:07,838
our very first time meeting,

5
00:00:07,838 --> 00:00:10,189
so why talk about your sins being
forgiven?

6
00:00:10,189 --> 00:00:11,757
Now, there's a picture next to me,

7
00:00:11,757 --> 00:00:12,933
an image beside me,

8
00:00:12,933 --> 00:00:14,500
and that image, in fact,

9
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,460
comes from this book right here.

10
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:19,007
I don't know if you can see, here in my
hand,

11
00:00:19,007 --> 00:00:20,770
I'm holding this book right now.

12
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:21,946
And this book —

13
00:00:21,946 --> 00:00:24,298
well, I doubt many people could read it,

14
00:00:24,298 --> 00:00:26,845
because it's written in Nepali.

15
00:00:26,845 --> 00:00:29,392
I bought it over in Kathmandu,

16
00:00:29,392 --> 00:00:29,980
and so,

17
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,380
this here is an event from the Lord Jesus'
life on earth.

18
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:37,160
We'll have a chance to talk about it a
little later.

19
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:42,280
Just now, after you heard Killy,

20
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,940
and after you heard Sai-fai share,

21
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:46,380
I wonder if you envy the change in their
lives.

22
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:50,920
It makes me think of this one verse in the
Bible.

23
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:51,840
What does it say?

24
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,420
It is the One who girds us with strength,

25
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:56,880
and makes our way perfect;

26
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:57,480
He is God.

27
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:03,120
The God we come to know today isn't just a
doctrine — He is a living Person.

28
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:06,440
Some people say you become like the
company you keep.

29
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:12,320
You'll find that those who believe in God
have changed lives, real experiences,

30
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:17,960
and they change for the better. From this
you see God is not only real, but good.

31
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:22,560
He is the One who girds us with strength
and makes our way perfect.

32
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:27,560
And I hope that today, through coming to
know this God,

33
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:29,560
your life, too, will be changed like this.

34
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:35,560
On my desk there's an ornament

35
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:38,560
that constantly reminds me how real God
is.

36
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:42,560
Can you see what I'm holding in my hand?

37
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,560
It might be a little dark.

38
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:50,560
It's actually a magnetically levitating
globe.

39
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:53,560
Sometimes I buy little things as gifts to
myself,

40
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:57,560
and this globe — what does it remind me
of?

41
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:04,560
Well, long ago many people believed the
earth was flat.

42
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:08,560
In fact, to this day there's even an
International Flat Earth Society

43
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:11,560
that claims the earth is flat.

44
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:14,560
So the people of old used to say

45
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:16,560
that sailing the seas and racing horses
each carry their risks.

46
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:17,560
Why is that?

47
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,560
Why was sailing so dangerous?

48
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:21,560
Because they thought the earth was flat.

49
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:23,060
If you went too far out,

50
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:24,560
you would fall off the edge,

51
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,560
tumbling down like off a waterfall.

52
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,560
So the seafarers of old

53
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:31,060
would hug the coastline as they went,

54
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:33,060
sailing a while, then back to shore,

55
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:34,060
a while more, then back to shore,

56
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:35,560
never daring to cross the open ocean,

57
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:38,560
because they feared falling off that
waterfall.

58
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:40,560
And you'll notice —

59
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:43,560
when did people finally realize

60
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:45,560
that the earth is actually round?

61
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,560
Well, going back to this,

62
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,060
you see there are two pictures here.

63
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:52,060
Going back to the Greek era,

64
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:54,460
back to around 200 or 300 BC,

65
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:56,660
some people began to wonder and to reason.

66
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:57,060
What was it?

67
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:59,260
when they watched a lunar eclipse,

68
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:01,360
there was a shadow on the moon.

69
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,060
That is —

70
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:04,260
the earth was blocking the sun,

71
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:06,260
and the shadow it cast had a curve to it.

72
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:09,060
so they guessed the earth was curved.

73
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,060
For instance, others also noticed

74
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:11,560
that —

75
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,860
on the very same day,

76
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:14,660
in different places,

77
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:19,000
the shadows the sun cast were different.

78
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:22,420
In Egypt, the shadow fell straight down,

79
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,380
but a few hundred miles away,

80
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,700
the shadow fell at an angle.

81
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:29,760
So they guessed the earth was curved.

82
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:33,600
But when was it finally proven that the
earth is round?

83
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:35,900
It was actually in the Middle Ages, around
the 16th century.

84
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:40,260
So why are Columbus and Magellan so
famous?

85
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:44,360
Because their discoveries were made at the
risk of their lives.

86
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:52,360
Because on an ocean voyage, if the earth
really were flat, they'd set out and never
turn back.

87
00:03:52,360 --> 00:04:00,360
But in fact the Bible has a verse that
says this, in the book of Isaiah —

88
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:06,716
When was Isaiah written? Around the 700s
BC,

89
00:04:06,716 --> 00:04:09,649
about the time of China's Eastern Zhou,

90
00:04:09,649 --> 00:04:11,360
even earlier than the Spring and Autumn
period.

91
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:17,360
The Bible says this: God sits enthroned
above the circle of the earth.

92
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:22,360
So the Bible told us long ago — 2,700
years ago it already told us

93
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:25,360
that the earth is a great circle.

94
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:32,360
The original word carries the sense of
something solid, three-dimensional.

95
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:36,360
So some English versions render it "the
sphere of the earth,"

96
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:40,360
meaning upon the round globe of the earth.

97
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,359
Here's another example.

98
00:04:41,359 --> 00:04:45,853
People long ago thought the earth must be
hung up by something,

99
00:04:45,853 --> 00:04:47,601
held up by something,

100
00:04:47,601 --> 00:04:50,348
because if nothing were hanging it,

101
00:04:50,348 --> 00:04:52,096
nothing holding it up,

102
00:04:52,096 --> 00:04:53,594
it would just keep falling.

103
00:04:53,594 --> 00:04:57,839
But do any of you feel like you're
falling? No.

104
00:04:57,839 --> 00:05:00,087
So surely something must be hanging it,

105
00:05:00,087 --> 00:05:01,585
something holding it up.

106
00:05:01,585 --> 00:05:05,580
So you'll find that in myths all over the
world,

107
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,443
there are legends just like this.

108
00:05:07,443 --> 00:05:10,238
Some picture the earth carried on a
turtle,

109
00:05:10,238 --> 00:05:11,868
some on a great elephant,

110
00:05:11,868 --> 00:05:13,498
some on the shoulders of a strongman.

111
00:05:13,498 --> 00:05:16,526
Maybe, who knows, after holding it up so
long,

112
00:05:16,526 --> 00:05:17,691
he shifts a little,

113
00:05:17,691 --> 00:05:19,321
and then you get an earthquake.

114
00:05:19,321 --> 00:05:20,718
That's how it is in the myths,

115
00:05:20,718 --> 00:05:23,280
in the human imagination.

116
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:26,899
But the Bible tells us it isn't so.

117
00:05:26,899 --> 00:05:32,328
The book of Job is even older than the
Isaiah we just mentioned,

118
00:05:32,328 --> 00:05:37,153
perhaps 3,500 to 4,000 years ago,

119
00:05:37,153 --> 00:05:42,280
around 1,500 to 2,000 BC.

120
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:44,620
And the Bible has this verse:

121
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:46,748
He stretches out the north over empty
space,

122
00:05:46,748 --> 00:05:48,663
and hangs the earth on nothing.

123
00:05:48,663 --> 00:05:50,152
The Chinese doesn't quite capture it,

124
00:05:50,152 --> 00:05:52,280
so how does the English put it?

125
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,280
What does it say?

126
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:57,280
It says God "hangs the earth on nothing."

127
00:05:57,280 --> 00:06:00,280
That is, God hung the earth without
anything holding it up.

128
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:02,280
Isn't that remarkable?

129
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:07,280
So let me ask you: when did we learn the
earth truly hangs on nothing, held up by
nothing?

130
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:10,280
When did the solid proof actually come?

131
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:13,280
Not until rockets rose into space.

132
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:15,280
When the astronauts looked back at the
earth, they found —

133
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:17,280
why, there really was no great elephant,

134
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:20,280
truly no strongman's shoulders holding it
up.

135
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:24,262
And on top of that, there were the
expeditions to the North Pole,

136
00:06:24,262 --> 00:06:25,348
the expeditions to the South Pole.

137
00:06:25,348 --> 00:06:27,339
Even the farthest places were reached,

138
00:06:27,339 --> 00:06:28,606
and they found no rope,

139
00:06:28,606 --> 00:06:29,873
nothing hanging it,

140
00:06:29,873 --> 00:06:31,140
nothing holding it up.

141
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:33,568
Yet already, over three or four thousand
years ago,

142
00:06:33,568 --> 00:06:35,129
the Bible had told us:

143
00:06:35,129 --> 00:06:35,476
God —

144
00:06:35,476 --> 00:06:40,680
"He hangs the earth on nothing."

145
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:43,539
Here's another verse.

146
00:06:43,539 --> 00:06:47,668
It says: Have you, in your days, commanded
the morning,

147
00:06:47,668 --> 00:06:49,892
and caused the dawn

148
00:06:49,892 --> 00:06:51,480
to know its place,

149
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:57,680
so that by this light the earth is changed
like clay under the seal?

150
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:59,280
What does that mean?

151
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:03,247
It's describing the moment of sunrise in
the morning,

152
00:07:03,247 --> 00:07:05,797
as the ground grows brighter and brighter,

153
00:07:05,797 --> 00:07:09,480
and the light spreads like a seal pressed
into clay.

154
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:11,480
What am I talking about?

155
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:17,480
Do you know how people in the old days
made a seal impression?

156
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:24,480
They would carve patterns and letters onto
a stone cylinder,

157
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:29,480
then prepare a flat surface of clay,

158
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:32,480
and roll it across the clay.

159
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:36,480
After pressing, don't the patterns and
letters come out?

160
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:40,129
And that stone seal can print a second
time,

161
00:07:40,129 --> 00:07:41,345
a third time.

162
00:07:41,345 --> 00:07:45,480
That's how people back then made their
impressions.

163
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:50,980
So why is the sunrise like a seal on clay?
What is it really picturing?

164
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:55,480
You notice it grows brighter and brighter,
the darkness slowly receding,

165
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:59,480
and the changing of the earth is just like
that rolling seal,

166
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:05,480
as if to show us the earth, like a rolling
seal, turns — it rotates on its axis.

167
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:08,371
And not only does it rotate,

168
00:08:08,371 --> 00:08:10,849
it also tilts —

169
00:08:10,849 --> 00:08:13,740
tilted at 23.5 degrees.

170
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:20,840
What effect does that have? Well, because
of that 23.5-degree tilt, we get spring,
summer, autumn, and winter.

171
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:22,752
So in a couple of days,

172
00:08:22,752 --> 00:08:25,301
it will be the winter solstice in the
Northern Hemisphere,

173
00:08:25,301 --> 00:08:30,080
while in the Southern Hemisphere it may be
the longest day of the year.

174
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:33,580
Don't the four seasons make life colorful?

175
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:35,580
And they serve a practical purpose too,

176
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:37,830
because when the earth is tilted,

177
00:08:37,830 --> 00:08:41,080
you find many regions become warmer,

178
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,830
more livable for people,

179
00:08:42,830 --> 00:08:46,580
so the habitable areas increase a great
deal.

180
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:53,580
If it spun straight up with no tilt, the
middle would be scorching and the poles
freezing.

181
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:59,580
Why is the Bible so extraordinary?

182
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:04,580
It says so much about the earth and about
science,

183
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:06,580
so why is it so accurate?

184
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:09,580
Even ahead of what many would later
discover,

185
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:13,580
things only proven with evidence many
years afterward.

186
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:16,580
It's because the Bible is the word of God.

187
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:18,580
Just as the Bible says here,

188
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:20,580
All Scripture is breathed out by God.

189
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:22,580
The Bible is the word of God.

190
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:29,580
This heaven and earth was made by God, so
of course He knows every detail of it,

191
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:34,580
and so through the Bible God lets us come
to know these things.

192
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:40,580
So through all we've said, you can know
the One in the Bible is the true God,

193
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:45,580
and through the Bible we also come to know
how real the true God is.

194
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:48,660
And it's not only through the Bible.

195
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:54,020
You'll notice — when you have time, why do
people love to travel, to head out into
nature?

196
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:55,300
Because it's beautiful.

197
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:58,640
When you take in the created world, you
find it is —

198
00:09:58,900 --> 00:09:59,920
so grand,

199
00:10:00,420 --> 00:10:01,460
so wonderful,

200
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,240
so intricate,

201
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:04,780
so beautiful.

202
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:11,180
The Bible has a verse — what does it say?
It says: ever since the creation of the
world,

203
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:12,980
God's eternal power

204
00:10:13,220 --> 00:10:14,260
His everlasting power

205
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:17,080
and His divine nature — that is, what He
is like —

206
00:10:17,340 --> 00:10:18,860
are clearly seen.

207
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:20,920
Though unseen by the eye,

208
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:22,960
yet through the things He has made

209
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:24,240
they can be understood,

210
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:26,040
leaving people without excuse.

211
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:31,420
So through the created world — the more
you go outdoors and look around,

212
00:10:31,660 --> 00:10:33,200
you'll come to know God too. Why?

213
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:35,760
Because you see the world, and isn't it
wonderful?

214
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:38,840
It's like this watch you see in my hand
right now.

215
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,900
When you look at the watch, isn't it
beautifully made?

216
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:44,900
Surely someone designed it, someone built
it.

217
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:48,900
And the beauty of this world, its
intricacy,

218
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:50,900
is far more complex than this watch.

219
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,900
So when I look at this world,

220
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:56,900
I know there truly is a Designer, a
Creator.

221
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:59,900
And God truly did create all things.

222
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:04,900
Now there was once a survey

223
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:08,900
of some of the most eminent scientists of
the last few centuries.

224
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:10,900
What did that survey find?

225
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:16,900
Among the scientists surveyed, over ninety
percent believed in God.

226
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:22,900
So let me tell you — believing in God is
not rejecting science.

227
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:25,900
More than ninety percent of those
scientists believed there is a God.

228
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:29,900
Why? Because the more they researched, the
more they understood this world,

229
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:32,900
the more they realized there must be a
Designer, a Creator.

230
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:35,900
So believing in God today is in fact very
reasonable.

231
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:42,300
This study was even published in the
newspapers.

232
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:45,620
I wonder if you happened to notice the
news.

233
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:49,460
As we come to this point,

234
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:53,560
you'll find that the God we are speaking
of today,

235
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:55,860
the God recorded in the Bible,

236
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:57,920
is the Creator of heaven, earth, and all
things.

237
00:11:57,920 --> 00:11:59,460
He is not made by human hands.

238
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:03,040
As someone once put it, the true God is
the One who made man,

239
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:04,060
who made heaven, earth, and all things.

240
00:12:04,060 --> 00:12:06,620
A false god is made by man.

241
00:12:06,620 --> 00:12:10,200
And the Bible says false gods have eyes

242
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:11,740
but cannot see,

243
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:13,280
have ears but cannot hear,

244
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:14,820
have mouths but cannot speak.

245
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:18,900
They can't be bought or sold in the
market,

246
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:21,220
and they never go on sale.

247
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:25,300
Also, you just heard Killy's testimony,

248
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,580
and Sai-fai's testimony,

249
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:29,400
and you saw that God is kind and good.

250
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:37,280
Some people — say, in the triads — worship
idols and false gods.

251
00:12:37,280 --> 00:12:42,320
The gangsters pray that their whoring,
gambling, and drinking all go smoothly.

252
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:46,480
And funnily enough, the police station
worships the very same idol.

253
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:50,480
So when your robbery fails,

254
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:55,960
you might wonder whether the god you
worship tipped them off — turned informant
on you.

255
00:12:55,960 --> 00:13:02,960
So from this you can see: this God is the
Creator of heaven and all things, and He
is good.

256
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:10,960
The Bible lets us know: God is love.

257
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:16,960
God greatly desires that people receive
all His goodness, all His riches.

258
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:22,960
So He sent His only begotten Son — God
sent His only Son —

259
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:27,960
to let people know Him, and to help them.

260
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:30,560
Concerning the Lord Jesus coming into the
world —

261
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:33,560
there are many prophecies in the Bible.

262
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:36,260
As the word itself suggests, a prophecy is
—

263
00:13:36,260 --> 00:13:38,840
something that has not yet happened,

264
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:40,160
foretold in advance.

265
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:43,420
In fact, concerning the Lord Jesus' birth,

266
00:13:43,420 --> 00:13:47,120
the Bible foretold when He would come,

267
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,840
where He would be born,

268
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:50,040
and what He came to do —

269
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:52,420
over three hundred prophecies in all.

270
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:54,640
Their purpose is to let us know,

271
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:56,340
so that when the Lord Jesus came,

272
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:57,400
we would not mistake Him.

273
00:13:57,400 --> 00:14:00,020
He is the Savior God sent.

274
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:02,020
He is the Son of God.

275
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:04,020
Here is one example.

276
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:09,020
We know that at Christmas, coming soon,

277
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:11,020
where was the Lord Jesus born?

278
00:14:11,020 --> 00:14:14,020
In Bethlehem of Israel.

279
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:17,020
Now in the Old Testament book of Micah,

280
00:14:17,020 --> 00:14:20,020
around the 700s BC —

281
00:14:20,020 --> 00:14:23,020
that is, some seven hundred years before
the Lord Jesus was born —

282
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:25,020
there was already a saying like this.

283
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:26,020
What does it say?

284
00:14:26,020 --> 00:14:29,020
It says: But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah,

285
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:31,840
though you are little among the towns of
Judah,

286
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:33,620
out of you shall come One

287
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:34,900
who will come forth for Me,

288
00:14:35,420 --> 00:14:37,220
to be the ruler

289
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:38,500
in Israel,

290
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:40,020
whose origins

291
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:41,560
are from of old,

292
00:14:41,820 --> 00:14:42,840
from ancient times.

293
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,640
These two lines say it very clearly.

294
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:46,420
"Bethlehem Ephrathah" —

295
00:14:46,940 --> 00:14:50,520
"little among the towns of Judah" — so
it's a town, a place.

296
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:54,100
Bethlehem was originally a very small
town,

297
00:14:54,620 --> 00:14:57,440
but a King would come forth from it,

298
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:59,880
to be the ruler in Israel.

299
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:02,320
A king coming forth — that alone isn't so
strange.

300
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:06,260
Even a king emerging, small as the town is
—

301
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:09,540
a small town producing a king isn't
strange.

302
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:10,760
That could well happen.

303
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:12,760
But notice the very last line.

304
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:14,460
It says His origins

305
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:18,440
have existed from the very beginning.

306
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:22,020
Apart from God, who could meet this
condition?

307
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:24,840
Only the self-existent, eternal God

308
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,620
could meet it.

309
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:32,000
So from this verse we know that Bethlehem
would see not merely a king appear,

310
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:33,780
but what kind of King?

311
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:39,940
The Son of God entering the world, whose
origins are from eternity.

312
00:15:42,740 --> 00:15:45,060
When the Lord Jesus came to earth,

313
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:47,860
He went about doing good,

314
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:49,400
He performed many miracles,

315
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:51,200
and helped many people.

316
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:54,020
He made the blind

317
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:55,540
able to see.

318
00:15:55,540 --> 00:16:00,540
I wonder, at this stage of your life,

319
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:04,540
how much you've come to understand about
living.

320
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:07,540
Are you still groping about in the dark,

321
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:08,540
still lost and adrift,

322
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:11,540
not knowing what the meaning of life is,

323
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:13,540
not knowing what you're chasing after?

324
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:16,540
The Lord Jesus came and made the blind
see,

325
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:18,540
bringing light into our lives.

326
00:16:18,540 --> 00:16:23,540
He also once stilled the wind and the
waves in a storm.

327
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:26,100
He can rescue our lives,

328
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:28,140
and He can calm the storm.

329
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:31,740
In life you'll sometimes meet
circumstances

330
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:33,780
that press in on you like a storm,

331
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:35,580
leaving you unsettled,

332
00:16:35,820 --> 00:16:37,880
making you feel in danger.

333
00:16:38,900 --> 00:16:40,940
But the Lord can help you,

334
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:43,260
calming every storm within your heart,

335
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:44,540
and carrying you through.

336
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:46,840
He could also make

337
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:48,620
the lame walk.

338
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:54,000
He cast out many unclean spirits, setting
free those who were demon-possessed.

339
00:16:54,000 --> 00:17:00,140
Perhaps some feel their lives are bound up
by so many things —

340
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:05,260
some bad habits, a foul temper,

341
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:09,860
an unhealthy way of living, certain sins,

342
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:15,760
some perhaps troubled by evil spirits —
and you'll find the Lord can help with it
all, and set them free.

343
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:22,760
He even once raised the dead, giving life
back to people.

344
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:28,760
So besides fulfilling many of the Bible's
prophecies,

345
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:32,760
showing us He is the Savior God promised
to send,

346
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:37,312
through the very things the Lord Jesus
did,

347
00:17:37,312 --> 00:17:43,760
we also know He is the One God was
sending.

348
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:48,760
At the very start I mentioned this little
book.

349
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:51,760
What story does this little book actually
tell?

350
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:55,760
It tells of a paralyzed man and his
experience of being healed,

351
00:17:55,760 --> 00:17:59,760
recorded in the Gospel of Mark.

352
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:01,760
What happened in this account?

353
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:06,760
At the time, the Lord Jesus came to a
place called Capernaum.

354
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:09,760
From this too you can see the Bible is
real.

355
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:14,120
It doesn't say "long, long ago, far, far
away,"

356
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:15,640
all vague like that — no.

357
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:17,440
The place the Lord Jesus came to

358
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:19,240
was on the north shore of Galilee,

359
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:20,760
in the region of Capernaum.

360
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:26,920
By then the Lord had done many signs and
wonders, many had been helped, and His
fame had spread.

361
00:18:27,420 --> 00:18:31,780
He went into a house, and so many came to
Him that they crowded around Him,

362
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:34,340
until there was no room left, not even at
the door.

363
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:39,720
And there was a paralyzed man — paralyzed,
meaning he couldn't walk at all.

364
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:45,760
But how precious — he had four friends,
four men who carried him.

365
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:51,760
The paralyzed man lay on a mat, unable to
move,

366
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:53,760
and I find this quite meaningful.

367
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:57,760
I wonder if you've noticed that sometimes
a person's life

368
00:18:57,760 --> 00:19:01,760
is ruled by circumstances, as if he can't
govern himself —

369
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:04,760
wherever the mat is carried, that's where
he goes.

370
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:12,160
The four friends each took a corner and
brought the paralytic before the Lord,

371
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:14,360
hoping the Lord could help them.

372
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:17,360
But there were so many people they
couldn't get into the house,

373
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:21,560
so they went up onto the roof and tore it
open.

374
00:19:21,560 --> 00:19:28,360
They lowered the paralytic and his mat
down before the Lord.

375
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:33,360
You might say — they were allowed to do
that?

376
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:38,360
Let me show you what life was like for
people back then.

377
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:41,360
The houses people lived in looked
something like this.

378
00:19:41,360 --> 00:19:44,360
Notice the roof is just one story up,

379
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:48,360
and the roof was usually flat, used for
drying things.

380
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:53,360
There was a staircase outside leading up
to the roof.

381
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:58,360
So the four men carried the paralyzed man
up onto the roof.

382
00:19:58,360 --> 00:20:01,360
And what were those roofs like?

383
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:09,360
Back then they were simple: a few beams
laid across, covered with branches and
straw, then a layer of clay on top.

384
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:12,703
So after every rain,

385
00:20:12,703 --> 00:20:14,760
they'd take a stone roller

386
00:20:14,760 --> 00:20:16,560
to flatten it out,

387
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:18,360
and let it dry in the sun.

388
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:24,360
From this you can see how they were able
to tear open the roof, to dig through it.

389
00:20:24,360 --> 00:20:26,920
And by the way,

390
00:20:27,180 --> 00:20:28,460
you know, in English

391
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,000
there's a saying:

392
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:33,580
when it pours, they say it's "raining cats
and dogs."

393
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:35,880
What does that have to do with cats and
dogs?

394
00:20:36,140 --> 00:20:37,420
Well, it's something like this.

395
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:41,760
Because back then people's roofs were
usually topped with straw,

396
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,560
laid over the top like this.

397
00:20:43,820 --> 00:20:45,860
And many animals — cats and dogs —

398
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:47,920
would live up in that straw.

399
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:49,440
So when it rained really hard,

400
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:51,760
they'd all come washing and sliding down.

401
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:56,400
That's why heavy rain is called "raining
cats and dogs."

402
00:20:56,400 --> 00:21:01,760
So they tore open the roof and lowered him
down.

403
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:08,000
What did the Lord say?

404
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:12,000
The Lord saw their faith — notice that,
their faith.

405
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:16,000
That means not only the paralytic, but the
four friends as well.

406
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:20,000
Why did He see their faith?

407
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:23,028
Because you can see what they believed.

408
00:21:23,028 --> 00:21:26,756
They believed that if they just brought
the paralytic before the Lord,

409
00:21:26,756 --> 00:21:28,386
there would be hope for him.

410
00:21:28,386 --> 00:21:29,784
The Lord could help,

411
00:21:29,784 --> 00:21:32,579
so they even tore open the roof —

412
00:21:32,579 --> 00:21:35,142
at worst they'd repair it for the owner
afterward,

413
00:21:35,142 --> 00:21:38,170
and they didn't fear the risk of being
scolded.

414
00:21:38,170 --> 00:21:40,267
Braving the chance of a rebuke,

415
00:21:40,267 --> 00:21:44,460
they still tore open the roof to lower the
paralytic before the Lord.

416
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:46,460
You can see how much they wanted it,

417
00:21:46,460 --> 00:21:49,460
and how they believed the Lord could help.

418
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:51,460
Today the Lord can help you too,

419
00:21:51,460 --> 00:21:53,460
no matter what situation you're in.

420
00:21:53,460 --> 00:21:55,460
The Lord saw their faith,

421
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:56,460
and said to the paralytic,

422
00:21:56,460 --> 00:21:59,460
He said, "Son, your sins are forgiven."

423
00:21:59,460 --> 00:22:00,460
What does "Son" mean here?

424
00:22:00,460 --> 00:22:01,460
"Son" —

425
00:22:02,460 --> 00:22:03,460
a young lad.

426
00:22:04,460 --> 00:22:06,460
I find this quite meaningful.

427
00:22:06,460 --> 00:22:08,460
The Lord didn't merely forgive his sins.

428
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:13,460
You'll notice there's a warmth, a
tenderness in the Lord.

429
00:22:13,460 --> 00:22:16,220
saying, "Son, your sins are now forgiven."

430
00:22:16,220 --> 00:22:17,760
From this too you can see

431
00:22:17,760 --> 00:22:20,360
that some illnesses today,

432
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:23,560
and some troubles, are brought on by sin.

433
00:22:23,560 --> 00:22:30,060
Truly — for instance, why do some people
struggle with mental illness?

434
00:22:30,060 --> 00:22:32,860
Because sometimes they harbor resentment,

435
00:22:32,860 --> 00:22:35,660
they're angry, unwilling to forgive,

436
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:38,560
dwelling on it, brooding day and night,

437
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:40,560
and it ends up like this.

438
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:43,060
Some keep turning over how others wronged
them,

439
00:22:43,060 --> 00:22:46,900
some dwell on all kinds of lustful things,

440
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:49,720
and in the end it affects the body.

441
00:22:49,980 --> 00:22:51,500
So you see, sin

442
00:22:52,020 --> 00:22:52,780
can sometimes

443
00:22:53,300 --> 00:22:54,320
cause a person

444
00:22:54,580 --> 00:22:55,340
to fall ill.

445
00:22:55,860 --> 00:22:58,420
What did the Lord say? He said, "Your sins
are forgiven."

446
00:22:59,180 --> 00:23:01,240
At the time, many people really were
crowding around the Lord,

447
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:03,020
and there were some scribes,

448
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:05,840
scribes being those who copied out the
Scriptures.

449
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:09,420
They knew the Scriptures and knew God,

450
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:10,460
to some degree.

451
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:12,760
But a few scribes were sitting there,

452
00:23:13,060 --> 00:23:19,460
which shows they'd come early, or held
some standing —

453
00:23:19,460 --> 00:23:21,760
others couldn't even get in, yet they got
to sit here.

454
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:26,620
In their hearts they were reasoning — not
out loud — saying to themselves,

455
00:23:26,620 --> 00:23:29,960
Why does this man speak like this?

456
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:32,260
He is speaking blasphemy!

457
00:23:32,260 --> 00:23:34,300
For apart from God,

458
00:23:34,300 --> 00:23:36,620
who can forgive sins?

459
00:23:36,620 --> 00:23:37,900
What is blasphemy?

460
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:40,700
Blasphemy is presumptuous speech,

461
00:23:40,700 --> 00:23:41,980
speech that oversteps.

462
00:23:41,980 --> 00:23:46,980
If He cannot forgive sins and yet says
"your sins are forgiven,"

463
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:49,980
that is overstepping — that is blasphemy.

464
00:23:49,980 --> 00:23:54,980
So the passage explains it: apart from
God, who can forgive sins?

465
00:23:54,980 --> 00:23:58,980
Of course, only the One who executes
judgment,

466
00:23:58,980 --> 00:24:02,980
who has the authority to condemn a
person's sin,

467
00:24:02,980 --> 00:24:04,980
also has the authority to forgive a
person's sin.

468
00:24:04,980 --> 00:24:08,980
They were reasoning in their hearts —
perhaps just exchanging glances —

469
00:24:08,980 --> 00:24:10,980
but they said nothing aloud.

470
00:24:10,980 --> 00:24:12,300
But what does the Bible say?

471
00:24:12,300 --> 00:24:16,100
Jesus knew in His spirit that they were
reasoning this way within themselves,

472
00:24:16,100 --> 00:24:17,560
and He said to them,

473
00:24:17,560 --> 00:24:20,700
"Why do you reason these things in your
hearts?

474
00:24:21,480 --> 00:24:23,660
Which is easier — to say to the paralytic,
'Your sins are forgiven,'

475
00:24:23,660 --> 00:24:26,580
or to say, 'Rise, take up your mat and
walk'?

476
00:24:26,580 --> 00:24:30,720
Which of these two is easier to say?"

477
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:35,060
"But that you may know the Son of Man has
authority on earth to forgive sins" —

478
00:24:35,060 --> 00:24:37,320
then He said to the paralytic,

479
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:41,820
He said, "I tell you, rise, take up your
mat, and go home."

480
00:24:41,820 --> 00:24:47,520
I think from this passage you can see
several things.

481
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:49,200
First, who is the Lord Jesus?

482
00:24:50,020 --> 00:24:52,900
He actually knew the thoughts within
people's hearts.

483
00:24:52,900 --> 00:24:57,760
Perhaps they really were just glancing at
one another,

484
00:24:57,760 --> 00:24:59,960
and the Lord saw their reaction —

485
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:01,740
the Lord's heart may simply be very
perceptive.

486
00:25:01,740 --> 00:25:04,160
But what you see is this:

487
00:25:04,160 --> 00:25:07,240
even the reasoning within their hearts —

488
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:08,520
the "why —

489
00:25:08,760 --> 00:25:11,840
why is your saying that this young man's
sins are forgiven

490
00:25:12,100 --> 00:25:13,120
blasphemy?" —

491
00:25:13,380 --> 00:25:15,420
the Lord knew this doubt of theirs,

492
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:17,220
and the Lord put a question to them.

493
00:25:17,480 --> 00:25:18,760
He said to them,

494
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:22,340
is it easier to forgive sins, or to say,
"Rise, take up your mat and walk"?

495
00:25:23,360 --> 00:25:26,440
Let me ask you all: which of these two do
you think is easier to say?

496
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:31,300
For people, for me,

497
00:25:32,060 --> 00:25:33,080
perhaps for all of you,

498
00:25:33,080 --> 00:25:35,640
of course "your sins are forgiven" is the
easier one.

499
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:36,400
Why is that?

500
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:38,200
After you say it, are the sins actually
forgiven?

501
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:38,960
Who can tell?

502
00:25:40,760 --> 00:25:42,300
You can't see it; nothing seems to happen.

503
00:25:42,800 --> 00:25:44,600
You just say it, and that's that.

504
00:25:44,860 --> 00:25:47,420
Some people say it and leave it at that.

505
00:25:47,680 --> 00:25:49,720
So "your sins are forgiven" seems the
easier thing to say.

506
00:25:49,980 --> 00:25:52,800
But if you tell him to rise and take up
his mat and walk,

507
00:25:53,040 --> 00:25:56,380
and then the paralytic struggles for
minutes and still can't get up,

508
00:25:56,640 --> 00:25:57,920
well, that's trouble.

509
00:25:58,940 --> 00:25:59,960
Right away

510
00:26:00,480 --> 00:26:02,520
it tests whether your words are true.

511
00:26:02,520 --> 00:26:07,640
So for people, "your sins are forgiven"
might seem the easier thing,

512
00:26:07,640 --> 00:26:11,220
but in the Lord's heart, in the Lord's
eyes,

513
00:26:11,220 --> 00:26:14,800
forgiving a person's sin is actually the
harder thing.

514
00:26:16,600 --> 00:26:17,360
It is harder.

515
00:26:17,620 --> 00:26:19,920
We'll explain a little later why it's
harder.

516
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:25,040
But the Lord said: so that you may know —

517
00:26:25,300 --> 00:26:26,840
"the Son of Man" refers to the Lord Jesus
—

518
00:26:27,100 --> 00:26:29,660
the Lord has authority on earth to forgive
sins.

519
00:26:29,920 --> 00:26:31,960
So the Lord said to the paralytic,

520
00:26:31,960 --> 00:26:34,260
"Rise, take up your mat and walk."

521
00:26:34,780 --> 00:26:36,320
I think the Lord is truly so considerate.

522
00:26:36,560 --> 00:26:38,880
He told him to get up,

523
00:26:39,120 --> 00:26:40,660
and the paralytic really did get up,

524
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:42,720
picked up his mat, and walked.

525
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:48,600
The Lord wasn't fussing over the mat — as
if to say, you dropped this mat,

526
00:26:48,860 --> 00:26:52,440
it's dirty, take it with you, don't leave
your trash behind.

527
00:26:53,460 --> 00:26:57,300
As I said, the mat was like a circumstance
ruling over him; before, he was lame,

528
00:26:57,560 --> 00:27:01,400
couldn't walk — wherever the mat went, he
went.

529
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:05,900
But today the Lord enabled him to walk;
now he could carry the mat himself.

530
00:27:05,900 --> 00:27:10,700
No longer ruled by his circumstances, he
could now handle them,

531
00:27:10,700 --> 00:27:14,700
he could deal with them. Those who believe
in the Lord today are just like this.

532
00:27:14,700 --> 00:27:17,500
It's not that nothing happens to us in our
experience,

533
00:27:17,500 --> 00:27:20,100
but rather that all kinds of things happen
in life,

534
00:27:20,100 --> 00:27:23,200
and I'm able to handle them, able to deal
with them.

535
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:25,300
The Lord gives us this ability.

536
00:27:25,300 --> 00:27:29,700
The man got up at once, took his mat, and
walked.

537
00:27:29,700 --> 00:27:31,900
What did the people there record?

538
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:38,200
They were all amazed — astonished, taken
aback.

539
00:27:38,200 --> 00:27:40,200
Seeing it, they gave glory to God. Why?

540
00:27:40,200 --> 00:27:42,200
Because this was clearly a miracle.

541
00:27:42,200 --> 00:27:46,200
That is, if He had spoken blasphemy,

542
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:48,200
how could He then perform a miracle?

543
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:51,200
The Lord's clear performing of a miracle
proves

544
00:27:51,200 --> 00:27:53,200
that He truly had not spoken blasphemy.

545
00:27:53,200 --> 00:27:54,700
He was not blaspheming God.

546
00:27:54,700 --> 00:27:56,200
And if that is so,

547
00:27:56,200 --> 00:27:59,520
then the Lord truly does have authority to
forgive people's sins.

548
00:27:59,780 --> 00:28:01,320
So those people were amazed:

549
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:03,880
"We have never seen anything like this!"

550
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:08,240
They had never seen such a thing —

551
00:28:08,480 --> 00:28:10,280
not that they had never seen

552
00:28:10,540 --> 00:28:11,300
a lame man

553
00:28:11,560 --> 00:28:13,100
healed and made to walk.

554
00:28:13,600 --> 00:28:14,380
After all,

555
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:17,700
the Lord had already performed miracles
and healed many before.

556
00:28:18,220 --> 00:28:19,500
At the very least, those few friends

557
00:28:19,760 --> 00:28:21,040
had this kind of faith,

558
00:28:21,280 --> 00:28:25,380
believing that bringing the paralytic
before the Lord would bring healing and
help.

559
00:28:25,380 --> 00:28:29,300
So when they say, "We've never seen
anything like this,"

560
00:28:29,300 --> 00:28:32,860
it doesn't just mean a lame man walking,

561
00:28:32,860 --> 00:28:35,260
but that here on earth,

562
00:28:35,260 --> 00:28:42,660
God could actually grant a man the
authority to forgive sins.

563
00:28:42,660 --> 00:28:43,780
And by their own words,

564
00:28:43,780 --> 00:28:46,380
apart from God, who can forgive sins?

565
00:28:46,380 --> 00:28:49,300
But the Lord clearly performed a miracle,

566
00:28:49,300 --> 00:28:51,500
proving He truly can forgive sins.

567
00:28:51,500 --> 00:28:54,180
That means the One before their very eyes
was —

568
00:28:54,180 --> 00:28:56,180
the Son of God, God Himself.

569
00:28:58,660 --> 00:28:59,780
Do you understand?

570
00:29:04,320 --> 00:29:07,120
The Bible tells us God is not only love,

571
00:29:07,580 --> 00:29:08,620
longing for people to receive

572
00:29:09,020 --> 00:29:10,220
His goodness,

573
00:29:10,520 --> 00:29:11,580
His riches,

574
00:29:11,820 --> 00:29:12,480
His love.

575
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:14,780
The Bible also says God is light,

576
00:29:15,220 --> 00:29:16,920
and where there is light, there is no
darkness.

577
00:29:19,980 --> 00:29:22,880
You just said God is so real, so good —

578
00:29:22,880 --> 00:29:25,880
so why can't I feel Him, why can't I
experience Him?

579
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:29,880
Well, this picture explains the situation.

580
00:29:29,880 --> 00:29:32,880
God is still light, He is still love,

581
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:36,880
but today many people are cut off from
God,

582
00:29:36,880 --> 00:29:38,880
and what is this wall?

583
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:41,880
It's the sin they have committed.

584
00:29:41,880 --> 00:29:47,880
The Bible says our sins have separated us
from God.

585
00:29:47,880 --> 00:29:50,346
This thick wall,

586
00:29:50,346 --> 00:29:52,072
this wall of sin,

587
00:29:52,072 --> 00:29:54,291
has walled us off from God —

588
00:29:54,291 --> 00:29:55,770
not merely separated,

589
00:29:55,770 --> 00:29:57,250
but cut off completely,

590
00:29:57,250 --> 00:29:59,716
so that we cannot see God,

591
00:29:59,716 --> 00:30:01,195
cannot feel Him,

592
00:30:01,195 --> 00:30:02,675
cannot experience Him,

593
00:30:02,675 --> 00:30:04,894
and we ourselves are in great pain.

594
00:30:04,894 --> 00:30:05,880
Why?

595
00:30:05,880 --> 00:30:08,880
Because, cut off from the God of light and
holiness,

596
00:30:08,880 --> 00:30:12,820
life has no hope, lived out in the
shadows,

597
00:30:12,820 --> 00:30:14,320
carrying the burden of sin,

598
00:30:14,320 --> 00:30:15,920
weighed down by its heavy load.

599
00:30:15,920 --> 00:30:17,700
You see this man,

600
00:30:17,700 --> 00:30:19,500
bound by a chain.

601
00:30:19,500 --> 00:30:21,240
If you ask many people,

602
00:30:21,240 --> 00:30:22,420
do you want to be good?

603
00:30:22,420 --> 00:30:24,260
Do you want to stop cursing?

604
00:30:24,260 --> 00:30:25,920
Do you want to stop lying?

605
00:30:25,920 --> 00:30:28,580
Do you want to stop flying into a temper?

606
00:30:28,580 --> 00:30:30,020
Many people will tell you,

607
00:30:30,020 --> 00:30:30,640
of course I do.

608
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:32,920
Who wants to be bad?

609
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:34,560
But the problem is,

610
00:30:34,560 --> 00:30:39,560
once a person sins, he becomes a slave to
sin, unable to overcome it.

611
00:30:39,560 --> 00:30:45,560
There was once a man who cursed, and he
tried —

612
00:30:45,560 --> 00:30:50,560
he made a New Year's resolution to stop
cursing; one day fine, two days fine,

613
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:55,560
but before a week was out he was at it
again, even worse than before.

614
00:30:55,560 --> 00:30:59,560
You see, to sin is to be a slave to sin.

615
00:30:59,560 --> 00:31:03,920
And not only that — there are
consequences: sin brings death,

616
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:07,760
and after death, there is still the
judgment.

617
00:31:07,760 --> 00:31:14,160
You might say, I've never murdered or set
fires,

618
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:16,720
I've committed no crime, I have no record,

619
00:31:16,720 --> 00:31:20,800
I hold a certificate of good conduct —
that's how I could immigrate here to New
Zealand.

620
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:25,420
Murder, arson, rape, and pillage — those,
of course, are sins.

621
00:31:25,420 --> 00:31:27,980
But what does the Bible say sin is?

622
00:31:27,980 --> 00:31:31,300
Anything that goes against the conscience
is sin.

623
00:31:31,560 --> 00:31:32,340
It's a curious thing.

624
00:31:33,100 --> 00:31:36,420
Today may be the first time I've met you,

625
00:31:36,940 --> 00:31:37,960
but in your heart,

626
00:31:39,240 --> 00:31:40,780
you know that what I'm saying is true.

627
00:31:41,540 --> 00:31:42,820
You have a conscience.

628
00:31:43,080 --> 00:31:44,880
You know what's right and what's wrong,

629
00:31:45,380 --> 00:31:47,180
and these aren't things you learned from
books.

630
00:31:47,700 --> 00:31:49,480
You don't need to raise your hand

631
00:31:50,260 --> 00:31:53,320
and ask, "Teacher, is it wrong to cheat on
the exam?" You don't need to ask — you
already know.

632
00:31:53,840 --> 00:31:55,620
You won't ask your mother,

633
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:57,160
"Is it wrong for me to steal your money?"

634
00:31:57,160 --> 00:32:05,160
People have a conscience, and anything
against the conscience is sin.

635
00:32:05,160 --> 00:32:13,160
Some say, well, I'm a bit petty about
things, or I dwell on lustful thoughts,

636
00:32:13,160 --> 00:32:16,160
but I never acted on it, I didn't hurt
anyone.

637
00:32:16,160 --> 00:32:21,160
But one of the terrible things about sin
is that you can't take it back.

638
00:32:21,160 --> 00:32:25,160
That friend I mentioned who cursed —

639
00:32:25,160 --> 00:32:28,410
cursing while chatting with others came
easily,

640
00:32:28,410 --> 00:32:31,910
but once he got into a fight,

641
00:32:31,910 --> 00:32:36,160
and the reason for the fight was that the
other man had cursed at him.

642
00:32:36,160 --> 00:32:42,160
You see, one of the terrifying things
about the sinful mindset is this: you
can't reverse it.

643
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:46,518
For instance, a man dwells on lustful
things.

644
00:32:46,518 --> 00:32:49,291
Take some husbands —

645
00:32:49,291 --> 00:32:51,272
as the saying goes, "a man who isn't a
playboy

646
00:32:51,272 --> 00:32:52,460
in his youth

647
00:32:52,460 --> 00:32:58,560
wastes his youth," so he takes mistress
after mistress. But if his wife said to
him,

648
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:03,560
how would you like it if I had a lover,
and a second, and a third?

649
00:33:03,560 --> 00:33:11,060
You'd find he'd flare up in anger. You
see, the terror of sin is that he can't
turn it around,

650
00:33:11,060 --> 00:33:15,740
along with that mindset — that
self-centered mindset.

651
00:33:15,740 --> 00:33:19,740
So in English, sin is called "sin."

652
00:33:19,740 --> 00:33:24,940
S is for "selfish," I in the center — the
self at the center — and N, nothing else.

653
00:33:24,940 --> 00:33:32,060
And God is light, and He hates sin.

654
00:33:32,060 --> 00:33:35,652
We were just speaking of sin —

655
00:33:35,652 --> 00:33:41,040
besides separating a person from God

656
00:33:41,040 --> 00:33:42,840
and leaving him unhappy,

657
00:33:43,080 --> 00:33:44,360
it truly leaves life

658
00:33:44,620 --> 00:33:46,420
without hope.

659
00:33:46,680 --> 00:33:48,200
no way out. I recently saw a news story.

660
00:33:48,980 --> 00:33:50,000
What was it about?

661
00:33:50,260 --> 00:33:52,300
In Switzerland they invented a so-called

662
00:33:52,820 --> 00:33:53,580
machine to help people

663
00:33:53,840 --> 00:33:55,880
end their lives — a euthanasia machine.

664
00:33:56,400 --> 00:33:57,940
You'd find it very strange.

665
00:33:58,960 --> 00:34:03,060
Why would people take their own lives —
apart from those with terminal illness?

666
00:34:03,320 --> 00:34:04,840
Some people, perhaps, simply

667
00:34:05,100 --> 00:34:06,380
feel there's nothing left to live for.

668
00:34:06,900 --> 00:34:08,680
You lie down inside it,

669
00:34:08,680 --> 00:34:11,400
and soon nitrogen is released, and you
lose consciousness,

670
00:34:11,400 --> 00:34:12,360
and then you die.

671
00:34:12,360 --> 00:34:13,760
You might find it very strange —

672
00:34:13,760 --> 00:34:14,900
why, of all things to invent,

673
00:34:14,900 --> 00:34:16,500
would someone invent a machine for
suicide?

674
00:34:16,500 --> 00:34:18,620
From this too you can see

675
00:34:18,620 --> 00:34:21,400
the hopelessness people feel,

676
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:23,680
once they are cut off from God —

677
00:34:23,680 --> 00:34:26,480
that darkness with no way out.

678
00:34:26,480 --> 00:34:32,400
Earlier, while we were leading the hymn,

679
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:33,620
I mentioned this verse.

680
00:34:33,620 --> 00:34:35,260
It says: it is appointed

681
00:34:35,260 --> 00:34:37,080
for everyone to die once,

682
00:34:37,080 --> 00:34:40,280
and after death, the judgment. God is
perfectly just.

683
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:44,380
So the poor will die, but the rich will
die too.

684
00:34:44,380 --> 00:34:46,280
Those with millions will die.

685
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:50,840
The powerless and oppressed will die,

686
00:34:50,840 --> 00:34:54,580
but the oppressors, the dictators, will
die just the same.

687
00:34:54,580 --> 00:34:58,640
Everyone dies once, but death is not the
end of it.

688
00:34:58,640 --> 00:35:03,360
Each will be judged according to what he
did in his life.

689
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:06,160
The wages of sin is death,

690
00:35:06,160 --> 00:35:10,000
and all who sin are cast into hell.

691
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:11,800
Hell is a

692
00:35:12,040 --> 00:35:12,820
lake of fire,

693
00:35:13,080 --> 00:35:14,860
a lake of fire that is never quenched.

694
00:35:15,640 --> 00:35:17,160
There was a recent news story:

695
00:35:17,680 --> 00:35:18,200
someone

696
00:35:18,440 --> 00:35:20,240
took three hundred thousand photographs

697
00:35:20,500 --> 00:35:22,540
and assembled them into a single image —
this one.

698
00:35:23,320 --> 00:35:26,900
It's been called the clearest picture of
the sun ever taken.

699
00:35:27,660 --> 00:35:29,200
Three hundred thousand photos pieced
together.

700
00:35:29,960 --> 00:35:32,020
You see this ball of fire,

701
00:35:33,040 --> 00:35:34,060
burning for billions of years.

702
00:35:36,160 --> 00:35:39,428
If God can make a sun

703
00:35:39,428 --> 00:35:41,210
that burns for so long,

704
00:35:41,210 --> 00:35:45,964
then you can be sure God will, for all who
sin,

705
00:35:45,964 --> 00:35:48,043
prepare a place —

706
00:35:48,043 --> 00:35:48,935
hell,

707
00:35:48,935 --> 00:35:50,420
a lake of fire.

708
00:35:51,160 --> 00:35:52,664
In fact, in the Bible,

709
00:35:52,664 --> 00:35:54,356
the One who spoke most about hell is the
Lord Himself.

710
00:35:54,356 --> 00:35:56,236
He said, if your eye causes you to sin,

711
00:35:56,236 --> 00:35:57,928
pluck it out;

712
00:35:57,928 --> 00:35:59,432
it is better to enter paradise with one
eye

713
00:35:59,432 --> 00:36:01,500
than with both eyes to be thrown into
hell.

714
00:36:01,500 --> 00:36:08,920
If your hand causes you to sin, cut it
off; better to enter paradise without a
hand than with both hands to go to hell.

715
00:36:08,920 --> 00:36:11,740
But He doesn't mean you should actually
pluck out your eye or cut off your hand —
no.

716
00:36:11,740 --> 00:36:16,600
He means: whatever the cost, do not go to
hell.

717
00:36:16,600 --> 00:36:18,284
The Lord loves you dearly,

718
00:36:18,284 --> 00:36:19,406
He loves people,

719
00:36:19,406 --> 00:36:20,810
and He is saying,

720
00:36:20,810 --> 00:36:23,616
don't come to such an end,

721
00:36:23,616 --> 00:36:25,300
don't go to hell.

722
00:36:25,300 --> 00:36:32,140
So God sent His beloved Son, the Lord
Jesus, into the world,

723
00:36:32,140 --> 00:36:33,500
and most importantly —

724
00:36:33,500 --> 00:36:35,960
yes, He healed many people's diseases,

725
00:36:35,960 --> 00:36:37,500
comforted many broken hearts,

726
00:36:37,500 --> 00:36:39,980
changed many lives —

727
00:36:39,980 --> 00:36:41,960
but the most important thing of all

728
00:36:41,960 --> 00:36:43,840
is that, for our sins,

729
00:36:43,840 --> 00:36:46,600
He bore the punishment.

730
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:48,800
God is just.

731
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:50,820
He will by no means clear the guilty.

732
00:36:50,820 --> 00:36:53,620
If a judge found you guilty,

733
00:36:53,620 --> 00:36:56,620
and said, "I love you, so I declare you
innocent,"

734
00:36:56,620 --> 00:36:59,120
then something is wrong with that judge.

735
00:36:59,120 --> 00:37:01,620
That judge himself is at fault, that judge
himself is unjust,

736
00:37:01,620 --> 00:37:05,120
because he's covering for you, isn't he?

737
00:37:05,120 --> 00:37:07,620
So when God would forgive us,

738
00:37:07,620 --> 00:37:11,620
He had to do it in a way that was just.

739
00:37:11,620 --> 00:37:14,120
That's why, with the paralytic we spoke
of,

740
00:37:14,120 --> 00:37:16,120
when the Lord said, "Your sins are
forgiven,"

741
00:37:16,120 --> 00:37:18,120
it was in fact a very hard thing to say.

742
00:37:18,120 --> 00:37:22,620
Yet from the very start the Lord spoke to
him the hardest words,

743
00:37:22,620 --> 00:37:24,300
declaring that He was willing.

744
00:37:24,300 --> 00:37:26,300
When He said He forgave that man's sin,

745
00:37:26,300 --> 00:37:27,580
perhaps He already had in mind

746
00:37:27,580 --> 00:37:29,620
that one day, for him —

747
00:37:29,620 --> 00:37:32,300
for the sins of mankind — He would pay the
price.

748
00:37:32,300 --> 00:37:34,100
But the Lord Jesus' greatest,

749
00:37:34,100 --> 00:37:35,500
most important act was this:

750
00:37:35,500 --> 00:37:37,860
to bear the punishment for our sins,

751
00:37:37,860 --> 00:37:39,220
hanging upon the tree.

752
00:37:39,220 --> 00:37:40,260
So the Bible says

753
00:37:40,260 --> 00:37:41,740
He loved me

754
00:37:41,740 --> 00:37:43,300
and gave Himself for me.

755
00:37:47,740 --> 00:37:50,180
In the Lord Jesus' final days,

756
00:37:50,180 --> 00:37:54,180
He had done many miracles and much good,

757
00:37:54,180 --> 00:37:58,180
yet out of hatred and jealousy, people
hated Him,

758
00:37:58,180 --> 00:38:01,180
hating Him without cause, and sought to
destroy Him.

759
00:38:01,180 --> 00:38:05,180
They used many false witnesses to frame
the Lord,

760
00:38:05,180 --> 00:38:07,180
speaking many lies,

761
00:38:07,180 --> 00:38:10,180
claiming He had said things He never said,

762
00:38:10,180 --> 00:38:13,180
in order to force His crucifixion.

763
00:38:13,180 --> 00:38:16,180
Crucifixion was a most cruel punishment.

764
00:38:16,180 --> 00:38:23,680
Before He was nailed to the cross, they
wove a crown of thorns and set it on the
Lord's head,

765
00:38:23,680 --> 00:38:28,680
draped a purple robe on Him, mocking Him,
jeering at Him.

766
00:38:28,680 --> 00:38:35,680
As we said, "Bethlehem Ephrathah — out of
you shall come a ruler" —

767
00:38:35,680 --> 00:38:39,680
So you're the king? You're the one to
rule? Congratulations, they sneered.

768
00:38:39,680 --> 00:38:45,680
So they crowned Him with thorns, robed Him
in purple, and mocked Him,

769
00:38:45,680 --> 00:38:51,680
struck Him with their hands, spat in His
face — a terrible humiliation.

770
00:38:51,680 --> 00:38:53,680
What does the Bible say?

771
00:38:53,680 --> 00:38:59,680
Yet the Lord set His face like flint, for
He was determined to go through all of
this for us.

772
00:38:59,680 --> 00:39:06,680
Three nails fixed Him to the cross; and
before that, they scourged the Lord.

773
00:39:06,680 --> 00:39:11,680
The whip was a cat-o'-nine-tails — one
whip splitting into nine tails.

774
00:39:11,680 --> 00:39:13,680
An ordinary whip lands with a crack,

775
00:39:13,680 --> 00:39:17,680
but this one had bits of metal on the
ends,

776
00:39:17,680 --> 00:39:21,680
sinking into the flesh and tearing it out
in a bloody mess.

777
00:39:21,680 --> 00:39:23,680
The Bible says the Lord's back

778
00:39:23,680 --> 00:39:25,680
was like a field plowed by oxen,

779
00:39:25,680 --> 00:39:29,680
its furrows deep and long.

780
00:39:29,680 --> 00:39:32,680
There are records of this:

781
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:35,680
some people died from the scourging alone,

782
00:39:35,680 --> 00:39:37,680
because even their inner organs were
exposed.

783
00:39:37,680 --> 00:39:40,680
There's not much flesh on the back.

784
00:39:40,680 --> 00:39:43,520
They beat the Lord terribly.

785
00:39:43,680 --> 00:39:47,920
Why does it dwell on how severely He was
beaten?

786
00:39:47,920 --> 00:39:51,400
Because the governor at the time, Pilate,

787
00:39:51,400 --> 00:39:53,880
wanted to use this to win the crowd's
sympathy.

788
00:39:53,880 --> 00:39:55,540
He said to them,

789
00:39:55,540 --> 00:39:58,400
I find no fault in this Jesus,

790
00:39:58,400 --> 00:39:59,800
yet he had Him scourged,

791
00:39:59,800 --> 00:40:03,320
tormented until He hardly looked human,

792
00:40:03,320 --> 00:40:04,900
then brought the Lord Jesus out

793
00:40:04,900 --> 00:40:05,540
and said to them,

794
00:40:05,540 --> 00:40:06,880
Behold the man!

795
00:40:06,880 --> 00:40:10,220
He's already been beaten so severely.

796
00:40:10,220 --> 00:40:12,680
His aim was to stir the crowd's sympathy.

797
00:40:12,680 --> 00:40:14,720
I find not the slightest guilt in Him,

798
00:40:14,980 --> 00:40:17,040
I know it's out of envy that you handed
Him over,

799
00:40:17,280 --> 00:40:20,100
and I've already had Him beaten like this
— it should be enough.

800
00:40:20,620 --> 00:40:22,400
But those people were set on rejecting the
Lord.

801
00:40:22,660 --> 00:40:23,680
They would not have Him.

802
00:40:23,940 --> 00:40:25,480
They demanded He be crucified.

803
00:40:26,240 --> 00:40:29,320
So with three nails, a man of over a
hundred pounds was hung

804
00:40:29,840 --> 00:40:30,600
upon the wood.

805
00:40:34,960 --> 00:40:35,460
In fact —

806
00:40:35,980 --> 00:40:37,260
just imagine —

807
00:40:38,280 --> 00:40:39,040
He is the true God,

808
00:40:39,300 --> 00:40:42,640
the One who made heaven and earth; yet the
Maker of heaven and earth, in this world,

809
00:40:42,680 --> 00:40:44,980
could not find a single place to stand,

810
00:40:45,760 --> 00:40:48,320
hung between heaven and earth, reaching
neither.

811
00:40:50,360 --> 00:40:51,900
Rejected to such a degree.

812
00:40:53,940 --> 00:40:57,280
But there's meaning in it too — hanging
there between heaven and earth,

813
00:40:57,520 --> 00:40:58,560
so that today we

814
00:40:58,800 --> 00:41:01,360
might have a living way back to God.

815
00:41:01,620 --> 00:41:03,160
He became a ladder to heaven.

816
00:41:04,440 --> 00:41:07,000
Three nails held up a man of over a
hundred pounds.

817
00:41:07,260 --> 00:41:10,080
Naturally it was agony, the blood flowing
without stop.

818
00:41:10,080 --> 00:41:13,760
And when you're hung up like that, you
cannot breathe.

819
00:41:13,760 --> 00:41:15,540
Your weight pulls you forward,

820
00:41:15,540 --> 00:41:16,460
and you can't draw breath.

821
00:41:16,460 --> 00:41:19,680
So each time you breathe, you have to push
yourself up and back,

822
00:41:19,680 --> 00:41:22,420
but your back has been flayed open.

823
00:41:22,420 --> 00:41:24,180
Each time you press back,

824
00:41:24,180 --> 00:41:25,960
your raw back

825
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:30,100
scrapes against the splintered wood,

826
00:41:30,100 --> 00:41:31,840
so every single breath is agony.

827
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:33,860
With every movement,

828
00:41:33,860 --> 00:41:36,040
the wounds where the nails pierced

829
00:41:36,040 --> 00:41:37,440
tear wider and longer,

830
00:41:37,440 --> 00:41:38,420
wider and longer.

831
00:41:40,080 --> 00:41:45,080
He hung on the cross for six hours, from
nine in the morning until three in the
afternoon.

832
00:41:47,080 --> 00:41:50,080
And at noon, the sky turned dark.

833
00:41:51,080 --> 00:41:56,080
We spoke of that ball of fire, the sun,
burning so long —

834
00:41:56,080 --> 00:42:00,080
yet at midday, from twelve noon until
three in the afternoon,

835
00:42:00,080 --> 00:42:06,080
the Bible says darkness came over all the
land. Why?

836
00:42:06,080 --> 00:42:14,080
I find it striking: this was the darkest
hour in the universe — the One who least
deserved to die, dying;

837
00:42:14,080 --> 00:42:19,080
the One without sin, hung upon the tree
for us.

838
00:42:19,080 --> 00:42:25,080
This was no solar eclipse, for an eclipse
never lasts three hours,

839
00:42:25,080 --> 00:42:29,080
and besides, if you know that day was the
fourteenth of the month,

840
00:42:29,080 --> 00:42:35,080
the moon was not between the sun and the
earth; the moon was far off,

841
00:42:35,080 --> 00:42:38,920
with the earth in between — so it was no
eclipse.

842
00:42:39,940 --> 00:42:42,000
If you ask me why the land went dark,

843
00:42:42,500 --> 00:42:45,320
whether the sun withheld its light for a
time —

844
00:42:45,580 --> 00:42:46,860
I don't know the reason.

845
00:42:47,620 --> 00:42:51,980
But it seems to say something: God wanted
people to take note of one thing.

846
00:42:52,740 --> 00:42:54,800
Like on a stage, when the lights go out

847
00:42:55,300 --> 00:42:58,640
and a single spotlight falls on the
center, on the Lord —

848
00:42:58,880 --> 00:43:00,160
everyone must pay attention to this.

849
00:43:00,420 --> 00:43:01,700
As heaven and earth went dark,

850
00:43:01,700 --> 00:43:04,400
all people ought to take note of this:

851
00:43:04,400 --> 00:43:05,560
the Son of God,

852
00:43:05,560 --> 00:43:08,220
hung upon the tree for us,

853
00:43:08,220 --> 00:43:11,180
became a curse,

854
00:43:11,180 --> 00:43:13,720
bearing our sins.

855
00:43:13,720 --> 00:43:18,920
And at this point,

856
00:43:18,920 --> 00:43:22,400
I very much want to share a hymn with you.

857
00:43:22,400 --> 00:43:24,820
This hymn is called

858
00:43:24,820 --> 00:43:25,780
"Come,

859
00:43:25,780 --> 00:43:27,420
Come and Feel."

860
00:43:27,420 --> 00:43:31,200
I hope you'll take in the Lord's love for
you,

861
00:43:31,200 --> 00:43:36,200
His heart toward you — where His love for
you truly lies.

862
00:43:36,200 --> 00:43:39,200
He was willing to pass through every
suffering and hardship.

863
00:44:01,200 --> 00:44:08,140
God's love is displayed upon the cross;

864
00:44:08,140 --> 00:44:15,240
for me the Lord endured torment and scorn,

865
00:44:15,240 --> 00:44:21,900
shamed by men,

866
00:44:21,900 --> 00:44:26,800
heaped with slander.

867
00:44:26,800 --> 00:44:31,300
The Father's beloved Son tasted

868
00:44:31,300 --> 00:44:35,800
every mockery and torment,

869
00:44:35,800 --> 00:44:40,244
crowned with thorns,

870
00:44:40,244 --> 00:44:45,800
and cruelly scourged,

871
00:44:45,800 --> 00:44:50,164
His body covered

872
00:44:50,164 --> 00:44:54,800
over with wounds.

873
00:44:54,800 --> 00:44:59,244
Hands and feet nailed fast,

874
00:44:59,244 --> 00:45:04,800
hung high upon the wood,

875
00:45:04,800 --> 00:45:08,800
in utter agony —

876
00:45:08,800 --> 00:45:13,800
who can feel it?

877
00:45:24,800 --> 00:45:34,025
The pain

878
00:45:34,025 --> 00:45:54,780
that never ceases.

879
00:45:54,780 --> 00:46:00,040
His face gaunt and wasted,

880
00:46:00,040 --> 00:46:07,040
hung on the cross, His bones now all laid
bare,

881
00:46:07,040 --> 00:46:14,400
blood streaming down His face,

882
00:46:14,400 --> 00:46:19,040
dripping to the ground,

883
00:46:19,040 --> 00:46:21,400
sorely wounded,

884
00:46:21,400 --> 00:46:28,200
yet struck even by the Father.

885
00:46:28,200 --> 00:46:32,467
Who could write a poem

886
00:46:32,467 --> 00:46:37,800
to capture such love?

887
00:46:37,800 --> 00:46:41,978
His love,

888
00:46:41,978 --> 00:46:47,200
engraved within my heart.

889
00:46:47,200 --> 00:46:51,422
How fresh His mercy,

890
00:46:51,422 --> 00:46:56,700
deep and wide —

891
00:46:56,700 --> 00:47:00,700
the grace of the cross,

892
00:47:00,700 --> 00:47:05,700
who can ever fathom it?

893
00:47:05,700 --> 00:47:09,700
My Lord even

894
00:47:09,700 --> 00:47:14,700
cried out, "It is finished."

895
00:47:14,700 --> 00:47:18,300
I will ponder it

896
00:47:18,300 --> 00:47:23,700
ten thousand times over.

897
00:47:23,700 --> 00:47:28,144
Jesus, my Lord,

898
00:47:28,144 --> 00:47:33,700
Your love runs deep and will never die.

899
00:47:33,700 --> 00:47:37,700
This grace

900
00:47:37,700 --> 00:47:42,700
forever moves us.

901
00:47:42,700 --> 00:47:48,140
This deep grace —

902
00:47:48,140 --> 00:47:49,740
come,

903
00:47:49,740 --> 00:47:53,580
and feel it.

904
00:48:15,000 --> 00:48:21,923
He loved me and gave Himself for me.

905
00:48:21,923 --> 00:48:25,000
(Galatians 2:20)

906
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:38,000
As the hymn just mentioned, on the cross,
at the very end, the Lord cried out: "It
is finished."

907
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:42,680
He carried one purpose:

908
00:48:42,700 --> 00:48:43,980
to deal with our sins,

909
00:48:46,020 --> 00:48:47,300
to bear our sins,

910
00:48:51,140 --> 00:48:51,920
so that

911
00:48:52,180 --> 00:48:53,700
today our sins might be forgiven.

912
00:48:54,220 --> 00:48:55,760
He cried out, "It is finished."

913
00:48:56,260 --> 00:48:58,580
He had accomplished this salvation.

914
00:49:01,640 --> 00:49:02,920
It turns out that God,

915
00:49:03,940 --> 00:49:05,220
in just this way,

916
00:49:06,500 --> 00:49:07,540
set out to save us.

917
00:49:08,040 --> 00:49:10,340
The Bible says we, like sheep, have gone
astray,

918
00:49:11,120 --> 00:49:12,660
each turning to his own way,

919
00:49:12,700 --> 00:49:19,360
and God the Father laid on the Lord Jesus
the iniquity of us all.

920
00:49:19,360 --> 00:49:25,500
God used substitution to save you and me,

921
00:49:25,500 --> 00:49:29,080
crushing His own Son for us,

922
00:49:29,080 --> 00:49:32,240
making Him our sin-bearing Lamb.

923
00:49:32,240 --> 00:49:34,980
So the Lord Jesus is the Lamb of God,

924
00:49:34,980 --> 00:49:38,480
the holy One, without blemish,

925
00:49:38,480 --> 00:49:41,880
yet He hung on the cross for us.

926
00:49:41,880 --> 00:49:47,880
The Chinese character for "righteousness,"
if you look it up, falls under the "sheep"
radical.

927
00:49:47,880 --> 00:49:50,880
A lamb in my place — that is
righteousness.

928
00:49:50,880 --> 00:49:54,880
So that today we are not only free of sin,
but counted righteous.

929
00:49:54,880 --> 00:49:58,880
The Lord died in our place, and brought us
this gift,

930
00:49:58,880 --> 00:50:03,880
changing our lives, teaching us what is
lovely and what is good.

931
00:50:03,880 --> 00:50:09,640
How precious — the Lord, for us;

932
00:50:09,640 --> 00:50:11,100
and on the third day after His death,

933
00:50:11,100 --> 00:50:13,280
He rose from the dead.

934
00:50:13,280 --> 00:50:15,740
God raised the Lord from the dead.

935
00:50:15,740 --> 00:50:18,020
The Lord Jesus rose from the dead,

936
00:50:18,020 --> 00:50:19,340
and this declares one thing:

937
00:50:19,340 --> 00:50:21,320
this salvation has now been accomplished.

938
00:50:21,320 --> 00:50:23,920
If the Lord Himself had sin

939
00:50:23,920 --> 00:50:26,380
and died for it,

940
00:50:26,380 --> 00:50:27,740
He could never have risen.

941
00:50:27,740 --> 00:50:29,940
But the Lord's resurrection

942
00:50:29,940 --> 00:50:32,340
declares that He bore our sins,

943
00:50:32,340 --> 00:50:34,700
and that God accepted this work of
salvation.

944
00:50:34,700 --> 00:50:37,140
God raised the Lord from death,

945
00:50:37,140 --> 00:50:38,900
exalted Him with His right hand,

946
00:50:38,900 --> 00:50:41,900
and gave Him the name above all names.

947
00:50:41,900 --> 00:50:44,360
Today this risen Lord

948
00:50:44,360 --> 00:50:46,620
can help us walk the road of life,

949
00:50:46,620 --> 00:50:48,500
He can be with us,

950
00:50:48,500 --> 00:50:49,980
so my life is no longer lonely,

951
00:50:49,980 --> 00:50:51,880
no longer like duckweed adrift.

952
00:50:51,880 --> 00:50:55,080
He hears our every prayer,

953
00:50:55,080 --> 00:50:59,200
He can teach, guide, and change our lives,

954
00:50:59,200 --> 00:51:06,200
and bring us home — home to heaven, back
before the Father.

955
00:51:08,200 --> 00:51:14,200
Many people, coming to know this
salvation, have received the Lord as
Savior,

956
00:51:15,200 --> 00:51:18,200
their lives changed, their sins forgiven.

957
00:51:18,200 --> 00:51:20,200
How do you believe in the Lord?

958
00:51:20,200 --> 00:51:25,200
There's no paperwork to file; you need
only pray to the Lord sincerely.

959
00:51:25,200 --> 00:51:28,200
Lord, today I am willing to repent, to sin
no more.

960
00:51:29,200 --> 00:51:31,500
Forgive the sins of my whole life,

961
00:51:31,500 --> 00:51:34,580
and I am willing to receive You as my
Savior.

962
00:51:34,580 --> 00:51:35,860
It's as simple as that.

963
00:51:35,860 --> 00:51:39,440
The Lord is very glad to hear your prayer,

964
00:51:39,440 --> 00:51:40,980
glad to save you,

965
00:51:40,980 --> 00:51:42,760
glad to be your Savior,

966
00:51:42,760 --> 00:51:45,580
glad to walk life's road with you,

967
00:51:45,580 --> 00:51:50,200
glad to change both your life now and your
eternity,

968
00:51:50,200 --> 00:51:51,980
so that all who believe in the Lord

969
00:51:51,980 --> 00:51:54,800
have their lives changed for good,

970
00:51:54,800 --> 00:51:56,600
their sins forgiven,

971
00:51:56,600 --> 00:51:59,160
reconciled to God,

972
00:51:59,160 --> 00:52:01,200
becoming children of God,

973
00:52:01,200 --> 00:52:03,000
with abundant life.

974
00:52:03,000 --> 00:52:05,040
He said He came that people might have
life,

975
00:52:05,040 --> 00:52:07,600
and have it more abundantly —

976
00:52:07,600 --> 00:52:09,660
to enjoy true love,

977
00:52:09,660 --> 00:52:10,940
peace and joy,

978
00:52:10,940 --> 00:52:13,240
and a hope worth boasting in:

979
00:52:13,240 --> 00:52:17,080
that we have a bright and warm home in
heaven.

980
00:52:17,080 --> 00:52:19,380
Do you long to receive all this grace?

981
00:52:19,380 --> 00:52:23,220
This is what God has prepared for you,

982
00:52:23,220 --> 00:52:25,020
what God wants to give you.

983
00:52:25,020 --> 00:52:28,340
Why is this called the "gospel" — the good
news?

984
00:52:28,340 --> 00:52:32,940
It's because He is willing to deal with
our sins,

985
00:52:32,940 --> 00:52:38,580
and wants us to receive the greatest,
fullest happiness.

986
00:52:38,580 --> 00:52:42,160
At this point I'd like to give you all a
moment,

987
00:52:42,160 --> 00:52:43,960
to be still and think.

988
00:52:43,960 --> 00:52:48,060
If there are any here who have not yet
believed,

989
00:52:48,060 --> 00:52:51,120
who have not yet received the Lord Jesus
as Savior,

990
00:52:51,120 --> 00:52:56,760
I hope that in this moment you will make
this decision,

991
00:52:56,760 --> 00:52:59,320
to receive the Lord as your Savior.

992
00:52:59,320 --> 00:53:03,420
You can experience the Lord changing your
life,

993
00:53:03,420 --> 00:53:05,720
so that you are no longer in the darkness,

994
00:53:05,720 --> 00:53:07,260
but can enter the light —

995
00:53:07,260 --> 00:53:09,820
and a marvelous light at that.

996
00:53:09,820 --> 00:53:12,640
Believing in the Lord is a good thing.

997
00:53:12,640 --> 00:53:13,660
Don't hesitate.

998
00:53:13,660 --> 00:53:16,220
The people around you long for you to
believe,

999
00:53:16,220 --> 00:53:18,520
because as you change, as you grow better,

1000
00:53:18,520 --> 00:53:20,060
that is what they long for.

1001
00:53:20,060 --> 00:53:21,340
And when you believe,

1002
00:53:21,340 --> 00:53:26,200
they too can come to know the Lord through
your life in the days ahead.

1003
00:53:26,200 --> 00:53:30,560
I'd like to invite everyone willing to
believe today to pray with me like this.

1004
00:53:30,800 --> 00:53:33,120
You can pray in your heart,

1005
00:53:33,360 --> 00:53:36,440
or pray along with me, phrase by phrase.

1006
00:53:37,200 --> 00:53:37,980
Let's begin.

1007
00:53:41,820 --> 00:53:42,580
Lord Jesus,

1008
00:53:45,400 --> 00:53:47,440
I am willing to repent,

1009
00:53:49,240 --> 00:53:50,000
to sin no more.

1010
00:53:52,320 --> 00:53:53,840
I ask You to forgive my whole life,

1011
